# 4.7 Parametrization of Implicitly Defined Functions (Notes & Packet)

## Core Trigonometric Parametrization Rules

1. **Ellipse Parametrization**:
   $$\frac{(x - h)^2}{a^2} + \frac{(y - k)^2}{b^2} = 1 \implies \begin{cases} x(t) = h + a\cos t \\ y(t) = k + b\sin t \end{cases} \quad (0 \le t \le 2\pi)$$

2. **Hyperbola Parametrization**:
   $$\frac{(x - h)^2}{a^2} - \frac{(y - k)^2}{b^2} = 1 \implies \begin{cases} x(t) = h + a\sec t \\ y(t) = k + b\tan t \end{cases}$$

